 # Preconditions
 
-All new code should abide by `cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy`, and `cargo clippy --tests`.
-If your crate uses features, be careful to ensure that `clippy` is definitely being run on all of your code, for example by using `--all-features`.
+When Rust verification is required by the project, explicitly requested, or needed to verify a significant behavior change, use the repository's formatting and Clippy checks. Typical checks are `cargo fmt --check`, `cargo clippy`, and `cargo clippy --tests`.
+Include the feature-gated code and targets affected by the change using the project's supported combinations; use `--all-features` only when that combination is supported.
+Delegated workers leave checks to the parent unless assigned. Add tests only when requested or needed to reproduce an observed bug that existing tests miss.
+Check installed tools before running commands; installation of toolchains, components, or dependencies requires approval.
+
